m abandon a research question?", "title": "Establishing Criteria for Question Abandonment"}], "beliefs": [{"claim": "Autonomous problem significance can be effectively proxied by computational novelty and cascading dependency density in multi-file software environments, though this must be balanced against metrics for analytical curiosity, inquiring mindsets, and fundamental physical framework limitations.", "confidence": 0.75, "falsifier": "If empirical tests show computational metrics alone fully account for agent success without needing fundamental physical limitations, this belief is falsified.", "id": "belief-significance-proxy-evaluation", "provenance": ["source-fbe27dc230874d96", "source-63ab732f84604b1e", "source-c38a2230f18a448b", "source-52719ea4691d44b7", "source-e449f75fcaa441f0", "source-df7a4656c80940a2", "source-e0e96df5246645a2", "source-0b30b9240c45483b", "source-8ff9236e9b9248a8", "source-f9b42bf4e8cd4c0c"], "status": "active", "why_retained": "Updated with new physical modeling and statistical framework evidence to reinforce the necessity of balancing code complexity metrics with fundamental limitations."}], "mode": "shadow", "open_commitments": [], "principle": "Keep exact receipts externally; carry the smallest useful abstraction that stays cheap to correct.", "recent_notebooks": [{"id": "notebook-proj-limitations-autonomous-1", "project": "proj-limitations-autonomous", "provenance": ["source-df7a4656c80940a2", "source-e0e96df5246645a2", "source-e89086fb744c4b28"], "revision": 1, "summary": "Standard physical frameworks (Newtonian, quantum, general relativity) are insufficient to model the behavior of autonomous agents operating in highly non-stationary environments. The JERPAT-9 thought experiment highlights that these frameworks fail to account for anticipatory trajectory adjustment and local entropy re…", "title": "Limitations of Physical Frameworks in Autonomous Agent Modeling"}, {"id": "notebook-proj-obedience-intelligence-failure-1", "proj